--TEST--
Core\Crypto::seal and ::open without their Core\Crypto\Cipher argument are compile errors, because no algorithm argument in this class carries a default — `rule:core-api/tier-roster`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The other half of `crypto-seal-and-open-take-a-cipher-and-round-trip-under-each`.
// A cipher with a default would make the two-argument call below mean "whatever
// the library picked last", which is the `openssl_encrypt` failure one step up:
// the call site stops saying what it is under and a reader cannot tell. There
// is no default, so the shorter call does not compile at all.
secret bytes $key = Core\Crypto::generateKey();
bytes $sealed = Core\Crypto::seal("attack at dawn" as bytes, $key);
bytes $opened = Core\Crypto::open($sealed, $key);
echo "unreachable", "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: expected 3 argument(s), found 2
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
